     "value": "rank",
     "intent": "Deficiency: the operator list (residual_size, delta4, delta13, neg) contains no cross-sectional normalization, and all six seeds enter as raw features, so a heavy-tailed seed can earn pooled IC that is tail-driven. Indirect support: the only de-confounding transform in use, residual_size, is best on both mean_ic and icir in 4/4 probed seeds and keeps all 140 dates, while delta13 drops to 127. Mechanism: a monotone cross-sectional rank applied before mutation makes the IC tail-robust without a lookback warm-up. Expect |IC| and icir gains concentrated on the raw skewed seeds and no loss of n_dates. Uncertainty: the supplied evidence has no per-feature skew measure, so the deficiency is inferred from operator coverage, and it cannot separate rank from winsorize or zscore."
    }
   ],
